{title: No One Will Take Your Joy Away}
{subtitle: John 16:22}
{key: F}
{tempo: 95}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [F] | [F] | [F] | [Dm7] |
| [Dm7] | [Bb] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Are you discussing among your[Dm7]selves what I meant
[Bb]A little while and you will not see [Csus4]me [C]
[F]Again a little while and you will [Dm7]see me
[Bb]Truly truly I tell you this [C]truth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Dm7]You will weep [C]and mourn while the world re[Bb]joices
[Dm7]You will grieve but [C]your grief will turn to [Bb]joy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Now you have grief but [C/E]I will [Dm7]see you again
Your [Bb]hearts will re[C]joice in the [F]light [C]
[F]No one will take your [C/E]joy a[Dm7]way from you
Your [Bb]joy is com[C]plete and [F]bright
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When a woman is in la[Dm7]bor she has pain
[Bb]Because her hour has come at [C]last
[F]But when she has given birth to [Dm7]the child
[Bb]She no longer remembers the anguish [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Dm]Because of [C]her joy that a child has [Bb]been born
[Dm]Into the [C]world with such light
So [Bb]it [Dm]is with you in this [C]moment
Now you [Bb]have grief but I will [F]see you again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Now you have [C/E]grief but I [Dm7]will see you again
Your [Bb]hearts will re[C]joice in the [F]light [C]
[F]No one will take your [C/E]joy a[Dm7]way from you
Your [Bb]joy is com[C]plete and [F]bright
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]On that day you will [C]not ask me a[Bb]nything
[Dm]Whatever you [C]ask the Father in my [Bb]name
[Dm]He will give you [C]so your joy may be [Bb]complete
[Dm]I will tell you [C]plainly about the [Bb]Fa[F]ther
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
No one will take your [C/E]joy a[Dm]way from you
[Bb]No one will [C]take your joy a[F]way
{end_of_verse}

